ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITES OF SOFTWARE:
======================================
    Primary responsibilities of an entry level software engineer.
      1.Developing solutions.
      2.Testing and finalising solutions.
      3.Fixing errors.
      4.Coordinating and communicating with a team and other stakeholders.
      5.Learning and teaching new technologies and skills.


1.DEVELOPING SOLUTIONS:
=======================
   1.Understand the task that is being asked by you.
   2.Review existing documantation of the topic.
   3.propose an approach to solve the task.
   4.Ask questions as needed to clarity ask.
   5.Use coding best practices and design patterns (eg: naming conventions, track changes, version control, consistency throughout code, make code self-explanatory).
   6.Write code needed for solution.
   7.Reuse code when appropriate.

2.TESTING AND FINALISING SOLUTIONS:
===================================
   1.Use a DevOps approach to make code reviwes along the coding process.
   2.Have a knowledge of/be willing to self-teach about tests(eg : unit testing)
   3.Track code production (eg: APM(APPLICATION PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT) to track systems and descover error)
   4.Test Soultions across different softwares.

3.FIXING ERRORS:
================
   1.Locate the code that contains error independentiy or with support from colleagues.
   2.Test the functionallity that has an error.(Runtime error)
   3.Understand the technical details of the current error.
   4.Test the solution is working correctly.
   5.Test everything that can be affected ny the error(while system)

4.COORDINATING AND COMMUNICATING WITH A TEAM AND OTHER STAKEHOLDERS:
====================================================================
   1.Participate in and organise team discussions(eg: Sprint planning, Daily Scrum, Sprint Retrospective).
   2.Use team meetings as an opportunity to raise questions and problems(concerning your own/other's work).
   3.Define Situations in which it is acceptable to reach out to a colleagues for help vs independent problem solving.
   4.Find trusted contact persons who are willing to help.
   5.Identify desired ways of support provided by selected contact persons(eg: pair programming, online chat tools like Stack, reviews on Github, etc...)

5.LEARNING AND TEACHING NEW TECHNOLOGIES AND SKILLS:
====================================================
   1.Have knowledge of/be willing to self-teach about programming language (object oriented & functional development)and any other needed tool.

